Z||000004||loafer87gt||02-07-2000||11:46 PM||||i have been into computer graphics since i was a little kid. I started with Geopaint on my old commodore 64, then moved up to an Amiga. I used several 3D progs on this platform, and loved the Deluxe Paint program. I eventually moved on to the PC and am using 3D Studio Max 3 , Lightscape 3.2 and Photoshop 5.5. I do architectural design renderings for several firms up here in Canada. Last fall, I actually was contracted to do the 3D design renderings for the new Particle Accelerator Synchrotron project being built in Saskatoon. I was pretty proud of this because there is only two of these facilities in North America!! I started a 3d model of my 87 GT a while back, but haven't had enough time to finish it off. When I get it done, I'll let you guys know and you can take a peek at it. Did any of you other guys ever use an Amiga computer? Boy did I love those, had a 2000,3000, and 4000. Way ahead of their time IMHO.||||reg||1
